# Allowlist for scripts/ci/no-private-refs.sh — a security decision, not a convenience.
#
# One rule per line, `path/glob:pattern  # justification`. The glob matches the repo-relative
# path; the pattern is an ERE matched against the whole `git grep` hit (`path:line:text`).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. A justification is mandatory in review.
#
# ⛔ Do NOT add an entry to keep a real internal hostname, address or private repository path
# in a public tree. Remove it instead. An entry is only for a string that *looks* private but
# is not: a documented loopback example, a placeholder, or a term that collides with a rule.
#
# The guard and this file necessarily spell the patterns out; the guard excludes both from
# its own scan. Everything else is scanned.

# ── the Kubernetes cluster domain ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `svc.cluster.local` is cluster DNS, not estate topology: it is the same string
# in every Kubernetes cluster in the world and names no organisation, service or
# namespace by itself. This service must strip it to normalise an in-mesh
# authority, so the constant has to exist in source. The hosts that used to sit
# in front of it (named services and namespaces) were removed on 2026-11-14 and
# now come from deployment configuration; only the suffix remains.

src/main.py:for suffix in.*svc\.cluster\.local
src/main.py:host\.endswith.*svc\.cluster\.local

# A SYNTHETIC host whose left-hand label is the placeholder `x`, used to pin the
# no_host branch of `_normalize_authority`/`_check_app_host`. Names no real
# service and no real namespace; the left-hand label is what makes it synthetic.
tests/test_main.py:x\.svc\.cluster\.local
